cyw43-driver: release the gSPI WAKE_UP bit while the bus sleeps

Adds the compile option CYW43_SPI_RELEASE_WAKE_UP_ON_SLEEP (default 0, so
nothing changes for other projects). With it set, cyw43_ll_bus_sleep(true)
clears SPI_BUS_CONTROL bit 7 (WAKE_UP) after KSO off, and
cyw43_ll_bus_sleep(false) sets it again before KSO on. While WAKE_UP is set
the CYW43439 keeps its crystal running and cannot reach deep sleep.

Applies to cyw43-driver v1.1.1 (pico-sdk 2.3.1, lib/cyw43-driver):
    git -C "$PICO_SDK_PATH/lib/cyw43-driver" apply <this file>

